      "hook": "Catherine in a dark burgundy gown turns from the window with a cold smirk and says, \"Two words, and that healer's crown rolls right back into the gutter where it belongs.\"",
      "cliffhanger": "Catherine clenches her fist and says, \"Ten days is not a wall, Alexander. It's a door... And doors can be closed from the other side,\" leaving her counter-strike unnamed.",
      "why": "A villain monologue that opens on a threat against the heroine, builds a ticking clock, and cuts before revealing the plan.",
      "context_gap": "A stranger may not know who 'the healer' is or why Alexander has ten days."
    },
    {
      "title": "Send for the Priest",
      "start_block": "B023",
      "end_block": "B041",
      "hook": "Catherine grabs Agnes by both hands and hisses, \"Everyone in that chapel saw me humiliated today. Good. Let them remember it.\"",
      "cliffhanger": "Catherine presses a heavy coin purse into Agnes's hands and commands, \"Send for the priest. Tonight. And make sure no one sees him arrive,\" cutting before the priest appears.",
      "why": "Shows the villain weaponizing her own public disgrace and ends on a secret midnight conspiracy in motion.",
      "context_gap": "A stranger may not know what Father Thomas did in the chapel or why the priest is dangerous."
    },
    {
      "title": "Going Back Into That House",
      "start_block": "B027",
      "end_block": "B037",
      "hook": "Agnes whispers in alarm, \"My lady... the Duke has bailiffs watching every road out of the county,\" and Catherine smiles venomously.",
      "cliffhanger": "Catherine spins from the window and threatens, \"Then no one sees him. That is precisely your job tonight,\" cutting before the plan is explained.",
      "why": "A tense exchange that reveals Catherine is trapped yet still scheming, ending on a threat with no resolution.",
      "context_gap": "A stranger may not know who 'him' refers to or why Catherine is returning to the house."
    }
